From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jeongseok Lee <jeongseok@meta.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 13:54:10 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Support the macOS 11 SDK's Metal argument access enum

Filament 1.78.1 (google/filament#10356) sets MTLArgumentDescriptor.access
to MTLBindingAccessReadOnly, which first appeared in the macOS 14 SDK.
conda-forge builds against the macOS 11 SDK, where the same value is
spelled MTLArgumentAccessReadOnly, so alias it for older SDKs only.
---
 filament/backend/src/metal/MetalEnums.h | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/filament/backend/src/metal/MetalEnums.h b/filament/backend/src/metal/MetalEnums.h
index 0d42baa..3b24421 100644
--- a/filament/backend/src/metal/MetalEnums.h
+++ b/filament/backend/src/metal/MetalEnums.h
@@ -24,6 +24,12 @@
 #include <Availability.h>
 #include <Metal/Metal.h>
 
+// MTLBindingAccess first appeared in the macOS 14 SDK; older SDKs only have
+// MTLArgumentAccess, whose read-only value is the same.
+#if defined(__MAC_OS_X_VERSION_MAX_ALLOWED) && __MAC_OS_X_VERSION_MAX_ALLOWED < 140000
+#define MTLBindingAccessReadOnly MTLArgumentAccessReadOnly
+#endif
+
 namespace filament {
 namespace backend {
 
